<title>INDONESIA: Indonesian volcano quietens down.</title>
<headline>Indonesian volcano quietens down.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1997-01-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesia's most active volcano, Mount Merapi in central Java, quietened down on Saturday after emitting hot gas, lava and ash, volcanologists said.</p>
<p>Officials said on Friday thousands of people living on the volcano's fertile slopes had been evacuated to safety.</p>
<p>The official Antara news agency quoted the head of the Yogyakarta office monitoring Merapi as saying the 2,911-metre volcano was still spewing out gas and lava but the amount had eased off.</p>
<p>Mount Merapi, 400 km east of Jakarta, killed 60 people when it erupted without warning in November 1994.</p>
